      "title": "The gap this policy fills",
      "narration": "Gloria is 71 and lives alone. If arthritis or dementia makes it hard to dress, bathe or eat without help, who pays for her care? Medicare may cover a limited stay for skilled care, but it generally does not pay for ongoing help with daily activities alone. Medicaid can help people who meet Maryland’s financial and medical eligibility rules. Long-term care insurance can pay for help at home, in assisted living or in a nursing facility. Qualifying policies are an exception to some federal health insurance rules. Insurers consider age and health when they price coverage.",
