      "title": "How much, for how long",
      "narration": "Gloria chooses a daily or monthly benefit amount, say 250 dollars a day, matched to local nursing home costs. She chooses a benefit period, two, three, five years or longer; many policies express it as a pool of money, the daily benefit times the days, which lasts longer if she uses less than the maximum. She chooses an elimination period, often 30, 60 or 90 days of care before benefits start, which works like a deductible. A reimbursement policy pays actual charges up to the daily maximum; an indemnity policy pays the full daily benefit regardless of charges. Each choice moves the premium.",
