      "title": "Optional benefits",
      "narration": "Four options matter most. Inflation protection increases the benefit automatically, typically 5 percent compounded each year, so a 250 dollar benefit bought today still buys a day of care twenty years from now; Maryland insurers must offer it. Nonforfeiture preserves some value if Gloria stops paying, usually a shortened benefit period equal to the premiums paid, and Maryland requires it to be offered. A guarantee of insurability option lets her buy more coverage later without new underwriting. Return of premium refunds premiums less claims at death. Exclusions cover pre-existing conditions for up to six months, war and self-inflicted injury, but never Alzheimer’s disease. Underwriting checks health, medications and cognition.",
